The transition property is a shorthand for a number of properties that are used to control the transition from one state to another of the animation.
The properties that control by the transition property are,

1) transition-delay: 500ms;  : It delays the transition by the specified time.
2 transition-duration: 4s;  : It is the total time taken by the transition. 
3) transition-property: all;  : This can be used to set a specific CSS property in the transition. By default it it set to 'all' means it applies all the properties to the transition.
4) transition-timing-function: ease-in-out;  : This property is used to set the effect in which the transition should occur like linear(same speed), ease-in(ascending speed), 
ease-out(descending speed) and ease-in-out(ascending then descending speed).

All these can be written using the shorthand property:
transition: all 4s 500ms ease-in-out;
